{"id":"n3-003","title":"～うとした (〜uto shita)","jlptLevel":3,"shortExplanation":"Express an action someone tried to do but couldn't; 'tried to', 'attempted to'.","longExplanation":"The ～うとした grammar point is used to express an action that someone tried to do but couldn't complete, for various reasons. The formation differs depending on whether it is used with verbs. This grammar point can be translated as 'tried to' or 'attempted to' in English.","formation":"Verb-う stem + とした","examples":[{"jp":"電話に出ようとしたが、相手は切ってしまった。","romaji":"Denwa ni deyou to shita ga, aite wa kitte shimatta.","en":"I tried to answer the phone, but the other person hung up.","words":[{"surface":"電話","vocabId":"1443840","reading":"でんわ"},{"surface":"に","vocabId":null},{"surface":"出よ","vocabId":"1338240","reading":"でる","baseForm":"出る"},{"surface":"う","vocabId":null},{"surface":"と","vocabId":null},{"surface":"し","vocabId":"1310720","reading":"し","baseForm":"する"},{"surface":"た","vocabId":null},{"surface":"が","vocabId":null},{"surface":"、","vocabId":null},{"surface":"相手","vocabId":"1401000","reading":"あいて"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"切っ","vocabId":"1384830","reading":"きる","baseForm":"切る"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"しまっ","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"しまう"},{"surface":"た","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[3,4,5,6]},{"jp":"彼は大声で話そうとしたが、言葉が出なかった。","romaji":"Kare wa oogoe de hanasou to shita ga, kotoba ga denakatta.","en":"He tried to speak loudly, but no words came out.","words":[{"surface":"彼","vocabId":"1483070","reading":"かれ"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"大声","vocabId":"1414300","reading":"おおごえ"},{"surface":"で","vocabId":null},{"surface":"話そ","vocabId":"1562350","reading":"はなす","baseForm":"話す"},{"surface":"う","vocabId":null},{"surface":"と","vocabId":null},{"surface":"し","vocabId":"1310720","reading":"し","baseForm":"する"},{"surface":"た","vocabId":null},{"surface":"が","vocabId":null},{"surface":"、","vocabId":null},{"surface":"言葉"